> Thanks to Robert Dege (author of the chg-mcutil script) for his help in
> getting an mcicap entry that works for my MSL5052. I'll probably keep
> working on an MRU robot variant of the tpchanger script but this will work
> for now.
> 
> This is my working mcicap entry :
> 
> mc0:\
>         :mc=/dev/changer/mc0:\
>  
> :nd#4:ns#50:dt=tape:dn=/dev/ntape/tape0,/dev/ntape/tape1,/dev/ntape/tape2,
> /dev/ntape/tape3:tc=msl5000
> 
> Note that the mcicap man page is misleading, at best, confusing the mc:
> and dn: devices. 
> 
> Further experimentation shows that a minimal entry is :
> 
> mc0:\
> 	:mc=/dev/changer/mc0:tc=msl5000
> 
> The number of drives, device names, number of slots are determined
> automatically.
