I have Tru64 UNIX 5.1B, which comes with CyberSafe GSS-API and Kerberos5 
client libraries (OSFSSOW2K subset). The version supplied is rather old 
and lacks (among other things) the ability to learn default realm form 
the DNS.

Are there any plans for a newer version being included in some newer OS 
release or as a part of a service pack?

I think it is nice to have Kerberos 5 and LDAP functionality built into 
the system, but I would also liek it to be a bit more up to date.

I know I can install Heimdal or even MIT, but none of them are 
thread-safe, although Heimdal users have not seen any trouble - unlike 
MIT users (multi-threaded OpenLDAP + MIT Kerberos had problems).

I'm aware of Tru64 going down the drain (a damn shame). Could we have 
more recent versions of LDAP and Kerberos as a parting gift?

Nix.


