Hi all,
Since moving to 5.1B PK2 some time ago, I've noticed that
the mcutil command-line options -e and -I no longer work.

e.g:

alf1_root> mcutil -M tl891 -I
mcutil error = 3 : operation is not supported by device

alf1_root> mcutil -M tl891 -e
mcutil error = 3 : operation is not supported by device


alf1_root> mcutil -M Neo2000 -e
mcutil error = 3 : operation is not supported by device

alf1_root> mcutil -M Neo2000 -I
mcutil error = 3 : operation is not supported by device

The relevenat contents of my /etc/mcicap file are:

#Overland Neo2000
Neo2000|neo:\
        :mc=/dev/changer/mc2:\
        :ae:\
        :bc:\
        :it=scsi2:\
