Managers,

First of all, many thanks to those of you who wrote me with suggestions on 
how to deal with this problem (Raul and Tommy esp.). I got a lot of 
valuable information on how to deal with devices under 5.1A.

Problem:

My problem was stated originally as a question on how to get 5.1A to create 
device files for the new LVD disk I added to the system. The disk was added 
to a new controller (!) and although the disk was seen at the firmware 
level, I couldn't get the system to see it when booted and so I couldn't 
proceed to label the disk, etc.

Solution:

As unsatisfying as this is, it turns out that the brand new 3X-KZPCA-AA LVD 
controller was faulty. More info following...

No matter what I tried I could never get the device to be fully recognized 
and even though the system once created the /dev/disk/dsk# files, I could 
not use them. The best I could get was this:

# bcheckrc
<snip>
dsfmgr: NOTE: updating kernel basenames for system at /
scp kevm tty00 tty01 lp0 dmapi dsk0 dsk1 dsk2 dsk3 floppy0 cdrom0 tape0
dsfmgr: NOTE: creating device special files for system at /
+dsk4a +dsk4a +dsk4b +dsk4b +dsk4c +dsk4c +dsk4d +dsk4d +dsk4e +dsk4e 
+dsk4f +dsk4f +dsk4g +dsk4g +dsk4h +dsk4h

# hwmgr show scsi -full -type disk
<snip>
HWID: DEVICEID HOSTNAME TYPE SUBTYPE OWNER PATH FILE VALID PATH
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
48: 6 disk none 0 1 (null)

WWID:0410002c:"SEAGATE ST318406LC 3FE1D3C3000072442RKH"

BUS TARGET LUN PATH STATE
---------------------------------
3 0 0 stale

# disklabel -z dsk4
disklabel: dsk4: No such file or directory

I still could not label the disk. However, someone suggested I check to see 
if any errors were logged. Since I was only booting into single-user mode, 
nothing was logged to /usr/adm/messages, but when I booted into multi-user 
mode I found:

Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: itpsa0 at pci0 slot 15
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: IntraServer ROM Version V2.0 (c)1998
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: contig_malloc: cannot find memory in saved list
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: ITPSA: can't allocate script memory
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: hba_dme_attach: (3/n/n) - hba 'itpsa' attach 
fail
ed.
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: cam_logger: SCSI event packet
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: cam_logger: bus 3
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: ccfg_simattach()
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: SIM Attach Failed, sim_init() reported FAILURE -
Retry.
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: itpsa_attach_instance: Failure status 
returned fr
om xpt_bus_register()
Aug 11 15:33:02 delphi vmunix: itpsa_confl1: itpsa0 attach failed


I Google'd this error and found reference to a problem with the controller 
(3X-KZPCA-AA -- LVD SCSI adaptor)

This is not satisfying at all, but it turns out that the controller was 
faulty. I replaced it and everything works perfectly.


Thanks everyone,
Richard



