I've had a couple of suggestions, which I cannot try out until the
weekend because I cannot take the system down until then.

1) In /etc/inet.local, add the line lan_config -i tu0 -s100 -x1 -a1 -m utp 

2) restart the machine into the boot prompt and look for 
>>> sh ew*
and set it to full duplex/100MPS by using
>>> set ew(x)_mode

Thank you to everyone who replied....there's far too many of you to
name personally!

